# A rule must not report a finding when a value in its message is undefined.
# Here AuditHelper has an unknown layer, so SV105 reports it, and SV102 does
# not. NoLayerEngine is registered without a layer, so SR001 reports it, and
# SV104 does not.
exits 1 specval check
cmp stdout check.txt

-- .specval.yaml --
-- .specval/data/services.yaml --
services:
  OrderManager: { layer: manager }
  OrderAccessor: { layer: accessor }
  NoLayerEngine: {}
-- specs/undefined.yaml --
specval: 1
id: UNDEF-1
kind: feature
title: A spec where a rule has an undefined value
summary: AuditHelper has an unknown layer. NoLayerEngine is registered without a layer.
acceptance:
  - { id: AC1, text: Covered. }
services:
  new:
    - { name: AuditHelper, layer: helper, purpose: Calls a service from an unknown layer. }
    - { name: NoLayerEngine, layer: engine, purpose: Is registered without a layer. }
calls:
  - { from: AuditHelper, to: OrderAccessor, op: Audit, covers: [AC1] }
  - { from: OrderManager, to: NoLayerEngine, op: Run, covers: [AC1] }
-- check.txt --
.specval/data/services.yaml:4 error SR001 NoLayerEngine has no valid layer (got "") (services.NoLayerEngine)
    fix: Set layer to one of: manager, engine, accessor, resource.
specs/undefined.yaml:10 error SV105 helper is not a layer (services.new[0].layer)
    fix: Use one of: manager, engine, accessor, resource.
1 spec(s) checked: 2 error(s), 0 warning(s)
